details:
(a) whether Government has formulated a long-term strategic blueprint to help India qualify for FIFA World Cup and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether the Ministry has conducted any assessment regarding the potential financial and macroeconomic benefits of a thriving football industry in India, particularly in terms of job creation, sports tourism and domestic manufacturing of sports goods;
(c) the State-wise details of dedicated football academies currently recognised and funded by the Sports Authority of India (SAI); and
(d) the concrete steps taken by Government to promote grassroots football development across the country, particularly in non-traditional States, during the last three years?

(a) whether Government proposes to formulate a National Childcare Infrastructure Policy to expand access to affordable, safe and quality child care facilities for children of working parents, particularly in urban and industrial areas;
(b) whether Government proposes to encourage the establishment of such child care facilities through public-private partnerships, employer participation and convergence with existing Government schemes; and
(c) if so, the details thereof, including the proposed implementation framework and timeline?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a review of the progress made towards achieving the national road safety targets and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the measures being taken to strengthen black-spot rectification, speed management and technology-enabled traffic enforcement for reducing road accidents and fatalities;
(c) the number of accident black spots and high-fatality National Highway stretches identified and rectified during the last two years, State-wise; and
(d) whether Government proposes to further strengthen its road safety strategy, including revised milestones and interventions to reduce road accident fatalities and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made under the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana (PMSGMBY), including the number of rooftop solar installations completed and the total capacity installed since the launch of the Scheme;
(b) the State-wise details thereof, including the number of beneficiary households and installed capacity in Haryana; and
(c) the estimated reduction in electricity bills, carbon emissions and peak power demand achieved under the Scheme?

(a) whether the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) has taken note of misleading front-of-pack claims made by food business operators regarding the nutritional or health attributes of packaged food products;
(b) whether Government has strengthened the provisions under the Food Safety and Standards (Labelling and Display) Regulations, 2020 and other regulations to prevent and penalise misleading front-of-pack claims and the details thereof; and
(c) the details of action taken by FSSAI during the last three years against such violations, including the names of defaulting food business operators, nature of violations and penalties imposed?

(a) whether Government proposes to strengthen India's energy security and reduce import dependence by scaling up coal gasification and coal-to-chemicals, so as to substitute imported natural gas, methanol, ammonia and urea;
(b) the estimated value of imports that could be saved and the benefits envisaged for the country from this transition;
(c) the progress made so far, the areas and coal blocks identified for gasification projects, and the incentives offered under the coal gasification mission; and
(d) the roadmap and targets set for gasified coal in the coming years?

(a) the progress made in extending India's Digital Public Infrastructure, including Unified Payments Interface (UPI), DigiLocker and other India Stack solutions, to partner countries;
(b) the number of countries with which agreements or partnerships have been entered into for deployment of such Digital Public Infrastructure solutions, along with the sectors covered thereunder; and
(c) the expected strategic, economic and diplomatic benefits accruing to India from international deployment of its Digital Public Infrastructure, including its impact on digital trade, fintech exports and cross-border digital cooperation?

(a) the number of youth registered on Mera Yuva Bharat (MY Bharat) digital portal since its launch, State-wise;
(b) the details of Experiential Learning Programs (ELPs) and internship opportunities made available through the platform to boost workforce readiness for our youth;
(c) whether any steps have been taken to integrate Artificial Intelligence (AI) features on the portal, such as automated resume builders or skill-mapping tools, to help young people find suitable opportunities; and
(d) the measures being taken to expand the platform's footprint in rural areas, smaller towns and aspirational districts to ensure balanced access to leadership training and community service?

(a) whether the Ministry, in coordination with the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY), the Ministry of Home Affairs and other concerned agencies, has put in place a coordinated mechanism to prevent and combat online Child Sexual Abuse Material (CSAM);
(b) whether Government has strengthened child protection mechanisms, including counselling, rehabilitation and support services, for children affected by online sexual exploitation; and
(c) whether the Ministry has undertaken digital safety and online child protection awareness programmes for children, parents, teachers and caregivers, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the difficulties faced by policyholders in obtaining settlement of health and life insurance claims;
(b) the insurer-wise details of claim settlement ratio, average claim settlement time, claim repudiation ratio and grievances received during the last three years;
(c) the major reasons identified for delay or rejection of insurance claims and the measures taken to address such issues; and
(d) the measures taken to improve transparency, accountability and ease of claim settlement for policyholders?

(a) the quality assurance mechanisms presently in place to monitor permissible limits of heavy metals in AYUSH medicines;
(b) the details of inspections, laboratory testing and enforcement action undertaken during the last three years against manufacturers found violating prescribed quality standards; and
(c) whether Government proposes to further strengthen testing, traceability and quality certification of AYUSH medicines, and the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has designed targeted initiatives to restore structural pride and address decades of institutional neglect regarding the socio-economic empowerment of the Sikh community;
(b) data on financial outlays deployed in the State of Punjab under PM-VIKAS scheme for preserving traditional Sikh arts, crafts and heritage institutions;
(c) the number of youth and women from the community benefiting from these special skill and entrepreneurship clusters; and
(d) whether Government has a dedicated future roadmap to expand infrastructure development for historic Sikh minority institutions to globally project their identity and contributions?

(a) the details of the growing global investments from major tech companies and domestic groups in India’s Artificial Intelligence (AI) data center sector;
(b) the manner in which the development of coastal data hubs and renewable energy access will strengthen India’s position as a global leader in AI; and
(c) whether Government is planning to bring a comprehensive National Data Centre Policy to incentivise the data centre development in India, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made under the PM Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) Scheme ;
(b) the number of micro food processing enterprises assisted, credit-linked subsidies sanctioned and beneficiaries covered under the Scheme, State-wise, including Haryana ;
(c) the details of One District One Product (ODOP) products identified in Haryana, along with the number of enterprises supported and assistance provided thereunder, district-wise; and
(d) the measurable outcomes achieved under the Scheme in terms of formalisation of enterprises, employment generation and enhanced market access?

(a) the progress made towards establishment of Bhartiya Antriksh Station (BAS), including the proposed timeline for development and operationalisation of its various modules;
(b) the major technological milestones achieved and those planned, including human spaceflight technologies, docking systems, life support systems and orbital infrastructure required for the Mission; and
(c) the details of long-term roadmap for BAS, including its proposed scientific research programmes, international collaborations and expected strategic and commercial outcomes?

(a) the total number of driver-partners (Sarathis) onboarded nationwide under the cooperative-led 'Bharat Taxi' initiative since its commercial rollout, State-wise;
(b) the comprehensive timeline for expanding this service to 500 cities and towns, and the specific phase-wise rollout schedule planned for tier-2 and tier-3 urban clusters; and
(c) the structural details of the zero-commission revenue model and the operational framework of social security benefits, including health and accident insurance, provided to registered cooperative members?

(a) whether the Ministry has assessed the feasibility for the inclusion of CDSCO approved Artificial Intelligence (AI) screening technologies for breast cancer under the National Programme for Prevention and Control of Non-Communicable Diseases (NP-NCD);
(b) the current timeline for updating the NP-NCD Operational Framework to transition from traditional clinical breast examinations to AI-assisted diagnostic protocols; and
(c) whether the Ministry has initiated pilot testing for the inclusion of Artificial Intelligence (AI) screening technologies for breast cancer under the National Programme for Prevention and Control of Non-Communicable Diseases (NP-NCD)?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the increasing use of unsubstantiated claims like natural, organic, eco-friendly and similar environmental claims on food and consumer products;
(b) the details of action taken by the Central Consumer Protection Authority (CCPA) against such misleading claims, including the names of defaulting companies and penalties imposed during the last three years; and
(c) whether Government proposes to introduce a strengthened regulatory framework, including digital traceability and verifiable certification for products making environmental or organic claims, and the details thereof?

(a) the total number of mineral blocks auctioned since the inception of the auction regime in 2015, State-wise, and the number of blocks operationalised so far;
(b) the revenue benefit accrued, and expected to accrue, to the Central and State Governments from the auction of mineral blocks;
(c) the manner in which the enhanced availability of minerals, including critical minerals, is advancing India's self-reliance and its vision of Viksit Bharat 2047; and
(d) the manner in which coordination with State Governments has been undertaken to accelerate the auction and operationalisation of blocks?

(a) the salient features of Government's proposed Artificial Intelligence Data Centre being established by the National Informatics Centre and the details of AI-enabled Parliamentary and legal databases proposed thereunder;
(b) whether Government proposes to develop similar sovereign domain-specific AI knowledge repositories for sectors such as healthcare, agriculture and education; and
(c) the details of roadmap prepared for leveraging such repositories to develop indigenous AI applications for governance and public service delivery?

(a) the salient features of India Semiconductor Mission (ISM) 2.0, including the major initiatives proposed to strengthen India's semiconductor ecosystem beyond fabrication;
(b) the details of the progress made under ISM 1.0, including semiconductor fabrication, Assembly, Testing, Marking, and Packaging/ Outsourced Semiconductor Assembly and Test (ATMP/OSAT) facilities, design ecosystem, investments mobilised and employment generated; and
(c) whether Government has identified priority areas such as semiconductor equipment, materials, design IP, research infrastructure and skilled workforce development under ISM 2.0, if so, the details thereof?

a) whether tourism sector is a key engine of economic growth, employment and soft power on the road to Viksit Bharat 2047, and Government proposes to significantly raise its contribution to national income;
(b) the estimated size of tourism sector at present and the growth targeted during the next five years, including its contribution to GDP, employment and foreign-exchange earnings; and
(c) the steps being taken to strengthen the tourism ecosystem including tourist infrastructure, connectivity, hospitality and skilling, digital and last-mile facilities and environmentally sustainable and responsible tourism?

(a) the trend of drug abuse and cross-border narcotics infiltration in the border State of Punjab over the last three years, and the steps being taken to ensure accurate and uniform reporting of drug-related data;
(b) the quantity of drugs seized and the number of persons arrested, convicted and imprisoned in connection with cross-border drug trafficking during the said period;
(c) the support extended by the Central Government, including deployment of anti-drone and surveillance technology along the border and assistance under the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan; and
(d) whether Government proposes a strengthened Centre–State framework to dismantle drug-trafficking networks?

(a) the steps being taken to modernise school-education infrastructure, including the setting up of smart classrooms in schools and colleges with particulars for the State of Haryana and the budget spent thereon and to upgrade teachers' skills, especially in artificial-intelligence-enabled education;
(b) whether any analysis has been undertaken of the impact of online and AI-assisted learning, alongside declining attention spans, on learning outcomes; and
(c) whether Government proposes to reorient school and college curricula towards critical thinking, communication and employability, while strengthening digital infrastructure in schools?

(a) the total value realised for creditors under the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code since its enactment and the improvement in recovery from stressed assets compared to the pre-IBC regime;
(b) the manner in which the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (Amendment) Act, 2026, including the creditor-initiated resolution process and group and cross-border insolvency provisions, further streamlines resolution and helps creditors realise value faster; and
(c) the impact of the IBC on reducing the non-performing assets of banks and on protecting the interests of investors and depositors?

(a) whether Government proposes to build on India's pioneering framework for regulating dark patterns to make India a global model for digital consumer protection;
(b) the specified dark patterns recognised, the awareness generated among consumers and the manner in which a consumer may lodge a complaint against their use; and
(c) the number of violations reported, notices issued to e-commerce platforms and other actions taken by the Central Consumer Protection Authority during the last twelve months?

(a) whether Government proposes to position India among the global leaders in advanced air mobility by enabling electric vertical take-off and landing (eVTOL) air taxis, including a phased pathway towards autonomous, pilot-optional flight, for short-distance urban and regional travel;
(b) the milestones achieved in framing the enabling regulatory architecture — vertiport standards, type certification and a national urban air mobility policy — and the timeline for the first commercial corridors; and
(c) whether any companies or startups have applied for license for development and operation of such services, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of National Skills Qualification Framework (NSQF)-aligned qualifications developed for the Orange Economy (digital content, AVGC and e-sports) since the notification of the National Programme on Artificial Intelligence (NPAI) Skilling Framework;
(b) the steps taken to integrate such digital micro-credentials into the Skill India Digital Hub (SIDH) to enable credit-stacking of short-term certifications into recognised diplomas or degrees; and
(c) whether any credit-transfer equivalence or academic recognition framework has been notified in coordination with UGC/AICTE and the details thereof?

(a) the steps being taken by Government to develop a Grey Water Economy, including promotion of treatment, reuse and recycling of municipal sewage and wastewater;
(b) the measures undertaken to increase industrial and urban utilisation of treated wastewater in place of freshwater sources such as rivers and groundwater; and
(c) whether Government is considering a water credit framework, including fiscal incentives or tax rebates linked to industries achieving high or 100 per cent utilisation of recycled water, to encourage large-scale adoption?

(a) the current status of Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) for the proposed expansion of the Namo Bharat (RRTS) corridors to Karnal and Alwar respectively;
(b) the specific timeline proposed for the final submission of these DRPs for approval of the cabinet during the current fiscal year;
(c) the estimated commencement date for these corridors; and
(d) the fiscal allocations earmarked for preliminary infrastructure development and land acquisition for these specific regional rapid transit extensions?

(a) the present operational status, scale of compute capacity and institutional access framework of Government-supported national Artificial Intelligence (AI) compute/GPU infrastructure made available to researchers, universities and Startups;
(b) whether the facility is integrated with India’s indigenous foundation model initiatives, including BharatGen, to enable students and young developers to build Indian-language apps, creator tools and AI copilots for education and digital creator economy; and
(c) the steps under the IndiaAI Mission to ensure fair allocation, data security and regional inclusion and to prevent an “AI-Divide” by providing subsidised or free GPU access to students and Startups, especially in Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities?

(a) whether Government has taken note of concerns regarding the applicability of Goods and Services Tax (GST) on expenditure incurred towards Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) activities under the Companies Act, 2013;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the impact of GST on CSR spending and its implications for corporate participation in social development initiatives; and
(c) whether Government proposes to consider waiving GST on CSR-related expenditures or allowing input Tax Credit (ITC) on such spending to encourage greater corporate contribution towards social welfare activities?

(a) the details of PMEGP, Mudra and other early-stage enterprise support schemes, including eligibility, loan limits, approval timelines and beneficiaries during the last three years;
(b) whether Government has examined difficulties faced by first-time young entrepreneurs in accessing small startup capital (?50,000–?5 lakh) due to lack of collateral, credit history and delayed approvals and the manner in which these schemes address this funding gap; and
(c) whether simplified compliance, mentoring or handholding support is proposed for youth and student founders starting micro-enterprises, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether there is a proposal to monetize underutilized railway assets by establishing ‘Viksit Bharat Tech-Retail Hubs’ that integrate AI-driven ‘Phygital’ retail spaces with Startup incubation labs;
(b) the details of the RailTech Portal, launched in February, 2026, and its role in providing 50 per cent development funding to youth-led Startups for deploying smart-commerce solutions in railway complexes;
(c) the status of deploying ‘Bhashini’ (multilingual AI) and edge-computing at the 1,300+ redeveloped stations to assist young rural entrepreneurs in global trade; and
(d) the timeline for the establishment of the first phase of these hubs as ‘City Centres’ to generate non-fare revenue through youth-led micro-enterprises?

(a) the details of the proposed data governance framework to incentivise data localisation through mirrored datasets for large-scale Artificial Intelligence (AI) training;
(b) the number of indigenous Startups supported for curating high-quality, anonymised and machine-readable domestic datasets in the healthcare and agriculture sectors;
(c) the status of the 'AI-OS' initiative to convert Artificial Intelligence into a public good through shared open-source code repositories; and
(d) the details of financial contributions required from firms deriving substantial commercial value from Indian data to support domestic Research and Development (R&D) in AI?

(a) the measurable outcomes of “Women in STEM” fellowships under Mission Shakti (Samarthya) in advancing participation of women researchers in frontier domains such as AI, quantum technologies, biotechnology and advanced materials as of 2026;
(b) whether the Ministry is collaborating with the Department of Biotechnology and allied agencies to support women-led deep-tech and genomics startups through SANKALP or similar incubation hubs, and the details thereof; and
(c) the status of the proposed “Nari Shakti Startup Fund” in providing equity-based support to women founders in Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities working on climate-resilient agriculture, health-tech and other frontier science innovations?

(a) whether Government has launched a nationwide free HPV vaccination programme for adolescent girls and if so, the details thereof including targeted age group, coverage plan and fund allocation;
(b) the delivery strategy proposed for administering the vaccine, including the role of schools, primary health centres, frontline health workers and State Governments in ensuring coverage; and
(c) the financial outlay, procurement and rollout strategy, along with the target set for completion of the vaccination programme, measures for awareness generation, informed consent and equitable access, particularly in rural and aspirational districts?

(a) whether Government has examined the issue of high trade margins in essential medical devices such as coronary stents and knee implants leading to elevated patient costs;
(b) the regulatory measures taken by the National Pharmaceutical Pricing Authority to prevent overpricing and ensure affordability of critical medical devices;
(c) whether Government is considering a “One Nation, One Price” framework or nationwide price cap for essential medical devices to curb profiteering in surgical procedures; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?
bpn

(a) the preparedness of Government to integrate the targeted 500 GW non-fossil fuel power capacity by 2030, particularly the rising share of solar and wind, into the national grid;
(b) the details of grid-readiness and stability assessments conducted to manage intermittency, variability and peak-load balancing without risk of outages;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen grid resilience, including transmission expansion, Green Energy Corridors, energy storage systems, smart-grid technologies, forecasting and real-time balancing mechanisms; and
(d) whether additional flexible or baseload reserve capacity is being planned to ensure reliable 24×7 electricity supply, along with the timeline thereof?

(a) whether, in light of the Economic Survey 2025-26 recommending higher taxation on Ultra-Processed Foods (UPFs), the Ministry is promoting reformulation, product diversification and healthier processing through its schemes;
(b) whether the Ministry has proposed any surcharge or “Health/Nutrient-Based Tax” revenues for strengthening nutrition supply chains such as fruits, millets, pulses and protein-rich foods for programmes like PM-Poshan; and
(c) the guidelines to prevent regulatory evasion or “nutrient camouflage” and the support being provided to MSME food processors to transition toward healthier products without excessive compliance burden?

(a) the current status, milestones and indicative timelines for India’s 6G development, including testbeds, spectrum strategy and global standard-setting participation under Bharat 6G Mission;
(b) whether Bharat 6G Alliance is incorporating Haptic Internet (internet of touch) and immersive spatial computing into the 2030 roadmap and how such capabilities woud enable use-cases like remote classrooms, skill training and tele-surgery; and
(c) the measures proposed to support indigenous IPR creation, semiconductor and device ecosystems and specialised skilling so that Indian startups and youth benefit from the emerging 6G economy?

(a) the steps taken under Mission Poshan 2.0 to combat "Hidden Hunger" caused by the rising consumption of High Fat, Sugar and Salt (HFSS) foods among urban and peri-urban children;
(b) whether the Ministry, in coordination with FSSAI, is developing a "Front-of-Pack Labelling" (FOPL) awareness campaign to identify "Empty Calories" in ultra-processed snacks;
(c) how the Poshan Tracker App is being upgraded to monitor "Lifestyle Malnutrition" (overweight/obesity) alongside traditional metrics like stunting and wasting; and
(d) the progress of the "Poshan Vatikas" initiative in schools to promote "Bio-fortified" natural alternatives to combat the micro-nutrient deficiencies exacerbated by fast-food dependency?
bpn

(a) the progress of Hub and Spoke model under PM-SETU scheme, specifically the number of Special Purpose Vehicles (SPVs) established where industry partners hold 51 per cent management control;
(b) the specific "New-Age" curriculum modules introduced for the Creator Economy Animation, Visual Effects, Gaming and Carrier (AVGC), Green Hydrogen and AI-Sovereignty across the 200 identified "Hub" ITIs;
(c) how the Anchor Industry Partners (AIPs) are being incentivized to facilitate "Production-Linked Training" where students earn while they learn on actual industry shop-floors; and
(d) the steps taken to integrate these upgraded ITIs with the "Create in India" Mission to support young freelancers and digital entrepreneurs?

(a) whether the Central Drugs Standard Control Organisation (CDSCO) has a dedicated regulatory pathway for rapid approval of AI-enabled Class C medical devices for early detection of breast cancer and tuberculosis;
(b) the status of the Secure AI for Health Initiative (SAHI) in benchmarking indigenous mammography and chest X-ray algorithms using Indian clinical data; and
(c) whether a roadmap exists to integrate such AI screening tools with the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission for point-of-care screening and diagnostics at rural Health and Wellness Centres?

(a) the details of the Startup/SME Growth Fund announced in the Union Budget 2026-27, including its structure and the proposed roadmap and timeline for rollout;
(b) whether Government proposes to expand eligibility to the “creator economy”, including digital entrepreneurs, content creators and independent freelancers operating as micro-enterprises; and
(c) the safeguards proposed to ensure equitable access for startups from smaller towns and first-generation entrepreneurs, including any mentoring, credit-guarantee or handholding support extended through the fund?

(a) the details of the India-EU Trade Agreement;
(b) the anticipated boost to the country's export;
(c) the sectors of economy which will benefit from the deal, the details thereof; and
(d) the provisions in the agreement benefitting Indian students, Information Technology (IT) manpower and services sector?

(a) whether the India–European Union (EU)Trade Agreement includes provisions or enabling frameworks relating to digital trade, cross-border digital services or technology-enabled commerce;
(b) the steps taken by Government to strengthen digital infrastructure, compliance platforms and cybersecurity standards so that Indian Startups, young professionals and technology-driven enterprises can engage effectively with European Union (EU) markets; and
(c) the initiatives undertaken to equip young talent with skills, digital tools and institutional support required for participation in emerging areas such as digital services, platform-based trade and technology-enabled exports under the agreement?

(a) whether Government has assessed studies predicting AI-driven job displacement;
(b) if so, the reskilling and upskilling budget specifically allocated for workers to be replaced by AI;
(c) the public-private partnerships established for large-scale workforce transformation; and
(d) the measures to create a future-ready youth workforce in AI-resistant sectors like healthcare, creative industries and sustainability?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken cognisance of the increasing misuse of fake profiles and impersonation of women on social media and dating platforms;
(b) the specific interventions being undertaken under Mission Shakti to address online gender-based violence, including deepfakes and non-consensual sharing of images;
(c) whether Government is considering the formulation of a digital rights or safety framework to safeguard the dignity, privacy and security of women online; and
(d) the details of awareness and outreach programmes being conducted to educate young women on digital privacy, reporting mechanisms and legal remedies against cyber harassment?

(a) the digital platforms and portals currently used by the Ministry for delivery of welfare schemes and services, including scholarships, rehabilitation support and skill-linked benefits;
(b) the number of youth beneficiaries who have accessed services through these digital platforms during the last three years, year-wise and scheme-wise;
(c) whether the Ministry has undertaken any assessment of digital accessibility, grievance redressal timelines and service delivery efficiency achieved through these platforms; and
(d) the steps being taken to strengthen digital outreach, awareness and last-mile access for marginalised youth, particularly in rural and aspirational districts?

(a) whether Government maintains or has commissioned any data or studies on the adoption of mental health and wellness leave policies by companies registered under the Companies Act, 2013, including sector-wise or size-wise trends;
(b) whether any review has been undertaken to assess the impact of existing corporate governance and labour frameworks on work-life balance, employee stress levels and productivity outcomes; and
(c) the details of advisories, circulars or guidelines issued during the last five years to promote healthy work environments, including measures for burnout prevention, stress management and employee well-being?

(a) whether Government has assessed the extent of delayed payments owed to Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) by large Corporates, PSUs and Government departments, particularly beyond the timelines prescribed under the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises Development Act, 2006;
(b) number of cases and total amount of dues currently pending on the MSME Samadhaan portal since last three years, year-wise;
(c) whether Government proposes to introduce stricter enforcement mechanisms, including automatic interest penalties or payment-linked compliance ratings, to deter chronic payment defaulters; and
(d) manner in which Government intends to ease working capital stress for MSMEs to prevent closures, job losses and supply-chain disruptions?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of rising urban heat stress and heat islands on public health, productivity and quality of life in cities;
(b) details of guidelines or advisories issued to States and Urban Local Bodies for adopting heat-resilient urban planning measures such as cool roofs, urban forests, water bodies and reflective infrastructure;
(c) whether provisions related to heat mitigation and climate resilience are being integrated into schemes such as AMRUT, Smart Cities Mission (SCM) and PMAY (Urban); and
(d) the steps taken and funding for city-level Heat Action Plans to protect vulnerable populations during extreme heat events?

(a) whether the Ministry provides any kind of support, monetary or otherwise to upcoming content creators, innovators, Artificial intelligence (AI) developers, Game designers, etc.;
(b) whether the Ministry is aware that the online platforms such as YouTube, Meta, X exercise their monopolistic practises against the interest of smaller content creators, if so, the steps taken towards IP Protection, fair practices, algorithmic transparency; and
(c) whether Government sees value in the micro-influencer economy adding upto the digital economy and roadmap for further enhancing the sector?

(a) the details of the India Artificial Intelligence (AI) Impact Summit 2026 which is scheduled to be held in February 26;
(b) the manner in which the summit will strengthen the AI ecosystem in the country and support AI Startups;
(c) the total number of pre-event and in-event sessions planned, major AI companies participating and global audience for the event; and
(d) the total number of AI based Startups in the country and how does this number compare to other countries?

(a) the specific sections of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 or NHAI Rules under which police officials are authorized to stop and fine two-wheeler riders on National Highways;
(b) whether the Ministry proposes to issue a "Standard Operating Procedure" (SOP) to State Traffic Police to distinguish between "Safe Riding Gear" and "Stunt Riding"; and
(c) the rationale for banning high-end motorcycles with advanced safety features from Access-Controlled Expressways while allowing old four-wheelers with lower safety standards?

(a) whether the Ministry has any framework for recognition of content creation skills, prompt Engineering, AI based development, gaming, streaming under the National Skills Qualification Framework (NSQF), if so, details thereof;
(b) if not, whether Government is planning to bring such framework for recognition of the above skills;
(c) whether the Ministry plans to bring in courses for content creation, video editing, AI generated content, Prompt Engineering, etc, if so, details thereof; and
(d) what steps have been taken by the Ministry to promote entrepreneurship avenues for content creators, AI developers, Prompt Engineers, Video Editors, details of such schemes?

(a) the details of retail F&O participation in the country in the last financial year and current year;
(b) the details of money lost by retail investors in F&O, investor profiles, cities etc;
(c) whether SEBI has taken cognizance of the "Gamification" of trading platforms where complex F&O products are marketed to youth like video games;
(d) whether Government plans to mandate a "Financial Health Warning" on the login screens of trading apps, explicitly stating "90 per cent of traders lose money"; and
(e) whether minimum income/ net worth criteria would be increased to activate F&O segments, tax losses and decrease leverage?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of the rising incidence of early-onset cancers and other non-communicable diseases;
(b) whether any age-disaggregated data on cancer prevalence, stage of diagnosis and survival outcomes for this demographic is being maintained under the National Cancer Registry Programme;
(c) the specific factors including lifestyle changes, dietary patterns, environmental exposure, digital habits and delayed health-seeking behaviour have been identified by the Ministry as contributing to these trends; and
(d) whether Government proposes to introduce targeted early-screening, awareness and preventive health programmes for young adults, particularly for breast, cervical, colorectal and head-and-neck cancers?

(a) whether the Ministry is aware that despite the 2017 Act, a very small percentage of health insurance claims in the country are for mental health;
(b) whether Government plans to direct Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDAI) to mandate "Cashless OPD Coverage" for therapy sessions, as mental health treatment is mostly outpatient, if not, whether the Ministry consider for cashless OPD coverage for therapy sessions; and
(c) the number of insurance companies penalized for rejecting mental health claims in the last three years?

(a) whether the DGCA has defined a "Reasonable Cap" on flight cancellation charges relative to the base fare;
(b) whether Government is aware that cancellation fees often exceed the base fare and fuel surcharge, resulting in near-zero refunds for passengers; and
(c) whether there is a proposal to mandate a 24-Hour Cooling-Off Period, where a customer can cancel a ticket for free within 24 hours of booking?

(a) the details of steps taken to transition India from a State-led space programme to a global 'Space Manufacturing Hub';
(b) the details of Technology Transfer Agreement done with private sector for SSLV; and
(c) the steps taken to ensure that the private sector captures a significant part of global share on satellite launch market?

(a) the expenditure incurred by Government towards development of North Eastern Region (NER) since 2021, year wise and State-wise;
(b) the major milestones achieved towards enhancement of road infrastructure, healthcare, education, civil aviation, power, etc; and
(c) the outcomes achieved, so far, and future plan for development of the region?

(a) whether the Kalka–Amritsar train service, which earlier operated for the convenience of residents of Kalka, Panchkula and adjoining areas, has been discontinued;
(b) if so, the reasons for and whether any review has been undertaken regarding the inconvenience caused to daily commuters, elderly citizens and Sikh pilgrims who frequently travel to Amritsar;
(c) whether Government proposes to restore or introduce a new direct train service between Kalka and Amritsar to reduce travel time and avoid the need for passengers to first reach Chandigarh railway station; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the expected timeline for re-operationalising the service?

(a) the number of sportspersons with special abilities, including blind and visually impaired athletes, currently being supported across various sports disciplines and States under the Target Olympic Podium scheme (TOPS) and Khelo India scheme;
(b) the steps being taken by Government to strengthen training facilities, coaching support for such athletes;
